## 1. Postman Collection: Food Delivery App APIs

**Collection name:** `FoodDeliveryApp_API_Tests`

**Base URL:** `https://your-api.example.com`


### A. List Restaurants

**Method:** GET

**URL:**
```text
{{base_url}}/restaurants
```

**Positive test — valid request**

```javascript
pm.test("Status code is 200", function () {
    pm.response.to.have.status(200);
});

pm.test("Response is an array", function () {
    const data = pm.response.json();
    pm.expect(data).to.be.an("array");
});
```

**Negative test — invalid city parameter**

```text
{{base_url}}/restaurants?city=InvalidCity999
```

```javascript
pm.test("Invalid city returns a valid response", function () {
    pm.expect([200, 400, 404]).to.include(pm.response.code);
});

if (pm.response.code === 200) {
    pm.test("No restaurants match the invalid city", function () {
        pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an("array").that.is.empty;
    });
}
```

